                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>We have included J J Godwin as well as the more frequent J J G.</p>
                        <p>This appears to be the son of Joseph and Harriet Godwin. When contact begins he calls with Harriet on a couple of occasions and Godwin notes his presence 
  at a couple of meals at Joseph's. John, the other brother, does not appear to have married and there is no mention of JJG at his funeral. There is, however,
  mention of Joseph, Harriet and three children, one of whom is assumed to be JJG.</p>
